WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.667 --> 00:00:03.567
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show," everybody.

00:00:03.567 --> 00:00:04.701
You're here. You made it.

00:00:04.701 --> 00:00:08.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.133 --> 00:00:10.100
Well, guys,
let's get to some good news.

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:11.734
Today gas prices in the U.S.

00:00:11.734 --> 00:00:16.400
hit a two-month low
coming in just under $4.50.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:23.601
That story again --
gas prices are still high.

00:00:23.601 --> 00:00:25.133
[ Laughter ]

00:00:25.133 --> 00:00:27.000
Yep, gas prices
are on the way down.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:28.968
This morning,
a White House aide said,

00:00:28.968 --> 00:00:30.133
"Good news, Mr. President."

00:00:30.133 --> 00:00:32.667
And Biden was like,
"Is today April 1st?"

00:00:32.667 --> 00:00:35.000
Of course,
Biden can't catch a break.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.434
Gas prices are finally down,

00:00:36.434 --> 00:00:40.968
but thanks to the heat, Gatorade
is now 7 bucks a gallon, yeah.

00:00:40.968 --> 00:00:42.968
I don't know if you've noticed,
but it is hot!

00:00:42.968 --> 00:00:45.367
It is hot.
-Yeah, how hot is it?

00:00:45.367 --> 00:00:47.400
-Not just here in the U.S.,
but there are record

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.734
high temperatures
all across the world.

00:00:49.734 --> 00:00:52.234
Seriously, it's so hot,
people on TikTok were slapping

00:00:52.234 --> 00:00:54.234
each other with tortillas
just for the breeze.

00:00:54.234 --> 00:00:56.133
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.133 --> 00:00:57.968
-Oy!
-Pshew!

00:00:57.968 --> 00:00:59.334
It's so hot right now,

00:00:59.334 --> 00:01:00.968
the Fantasy Suite
on "The Bachelorette"

00:01:00.968 --> 00:01:02.467
is just the back
of an ice-cream truck.

00:01:02.467 --> 00:01:04.501
Hey!
-Oh, hey, oh!

00:01:04.501 --> 00:01:07.067
Mr. Softee!
-Yeah, yeah, that's --

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:08.801
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.234 --> 00:01:13.167
It is so hot,
people are ordering Chipotle

00:01:13.167 --> 00:01:15.133
just so the E. coli
can give them the chills.

00:01:15.133 --> 00:01:16.667
That's what I'm saying.

00:01:16.667 --> 00:01:20.801
People are doing this
'cause that's how hot it is.

00:01:20.801 --> 00:01:22.701
All across Europe,
the heat is brutal.

00:01:22.701 --> 00:01:24.968
Today actually was
the hottest day in the history

00:01:24.968 --> 00:01:27.334
of the U.K.
at 40 degrees Celsius.

00:01:27.334 --> 00:01:29.234
Yeah, Americans heard that
and were like,

00:01:29.234 --> 00:01:30.968
"Yeah, we have no idea
what that means.

00:01:30.968 --> 00:01:33.033
Is that hot? Is that hot?"

00:01:33.033 --> 00:01:35.467
Yep, the heat has been breaking
records around the world,

00:01:35.467 --> 00:01:37.200
and we're all trying
to beat the --

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:38.801
[ Thunder crashes ]

00:01:38.801 --> 00:01:40.701
Oh, what --what is that?

00:01:40.701 --> 00:01:44.367
-Yeah, it's in my contract.

00:01:44.367 --> 00:01:47.801
If it gets above 95,
I get misted.

00:01:47.801 --> 00:01:48.834
-Oh, really?

00:01:48.834 --> 00:01:50.200
-I don't want to call you
a loser,

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:51.701
but you should get
a better agent.

00:01:51.701 --> 00:01:53.434
[ Thunder crashes ]

00:01:53.434 --> 00:01:54.701
-Wow.

00:01:54.701 --> 00:01:56.167
-Oh. Now.

00:01:56.167 --> 00:01:58.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:01.133
-Wow. You're getting --
-Yeah.

00:02:01.133 --> 00:02:02.868
-Does that feel good?
Does that feel good?

00:02:02.868 --> 00:02:04.767
-Yeah, now I'm cool!

00:02:04.767 --> 00:02:06.734
-Yeah! [ Laughs ]

00:02:06.734 --> 00:02:08.167
Yeah, you're
definitely cool, buddy.

00:02:08.167 --> 00:02:09.467
-My man!
-You're definitely cool.

00:02:09.467 --> 00:02:11.200
-I'm blind!
-Yeah.

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:13.501
[ Laughter ]
Some TV news.

00:02:13.501 --> 00:02:15.667
"The Bachelorette" is in
full swing, and if you --

00:02:15.667 --> 00:02:17.834
[ Cheers ]
Yeah. Oh, it's good.

00:02:17.834 --> 00:02:19.167
If you don't know, now you know.

00:02:19.167 --> 00:02:22.601
This season there are not one,
but two Bachelorettes.

00:02:22.601 --> 00:02:24.200
[ Audience oohs ]

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:27.200
It might sound weird
to date two girls at once,

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:30.400
but remember it is a show
about dating 32 guys at once.

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:32.167
So just remember.

00:02:32.167 --> 00:02:34.734
So, as of last night,
they're down to 21 guys.

00:02:34.734 --> 00:02:36.100
Yeah, and I gotta say,

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:38.434
my favorite remaining
contestants are...

00:02:38.434 --> 00:02:42.767
Jacob, James, Jason,
Johnny, and Jordan.

00:02:42.767 --> 00:02:44.501
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.501 --> 00:02:46.968
Just saying. I just --

00:02:46.968 --> 00:02:48.868
One more time.

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:52.767
That's James, Jacob,
Johnny, Jason, and Jordan.

00:02:52.767 --> 00:02:54.868
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.868 --> 00:02:58.100
Again, that's Jamie, Jamie,

00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:00.501
Jeremiah, Jamarcus, and Jordan.

00:03:00.501 --> 00:03:02.234
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:02.234 --> 00:03:04.100
And just so we're clear,

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:09.133
that's Jibbly, Jobbly, Jasobbly,
Bobobbly, and Jordan.

00:03:09.133 --> 00:03:11.300
And finally, one last time.

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:16.267
That's Ja, Jeh, Jer, Juh,
and I forget this guy's name.

00:03:16.267 --> 00:03:18.133
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:23.734
It was...

00:03:23.734 --> 00:03:26.033
Last night's episode
was pretty dramatic.

00:03:26.033 --> 00:03:27.267
In case you missed it,

00:03:27.267 --> 00:03:29.400
here's a re-enactment
with actual words

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:30.901
from the actual show

00:03:30.901 --> 00:03:33.300
starring me, Tariq,
and Questlove.

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:34.667
Guys?

00:03:34.667 --> 00:03:36.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:36.901 --> 00:03:39.033
♪♪

00:03:39.033 --> 00:03:40.968
-Thanks, Jimmy.

00:03:40.968 --> 00:03:42.501
I'll be playing Chris,

00:03:42.501 --> 00:03:45.767
a contestant
with nefarious intentions.

00:03:45.767 --> 00:03:51.067
-And I'll be playing Quincey,
who is about to confront Chris.

00:03:51.067 --> 00:03:53.234
-I'll be playing Jordan H.

00:03:53.234 --> 00:03:56.267
Alright. Let's get ready.

00:03:56.267 --> 00:04:00.767
-My personal perspective
is that if you're in a situation

00:04:00.767 --> 00:04:04.100
where there's four people
invited to this Fantasy Suite,

00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:06.434
and then the female
in the situation

00:04:06.434 --> 00:04:09.801
has sex with someone else,
then I wouldn't be interested

00:04:09.801 --> 00:04:14.467
in that person
being the person I'm with.

00:04:14.467 --> 00:04:17.467
-Would you vocalize that
to them before Fantasy Suites

00:04:17.467 --> 00:04:21.000
or during Fantasy Sites
or -- or after Fantasy Suites?

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:22.367
-Good question.

00:04:22.367 --> 00:04:25.634
Well, it would be dependent
on the situation.

00:04:25.634 --> 00:04:28.501
-Well, you wouldn't know
the situation.

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:31.133
-Listen. Listen.

00:04:31.133 --> 00:04:32.767
-You wouldn't know
the situation!

00:04:32.767 --> 00:04:35.667
-Gosh darn it!
I did not say that!

00:04:35.667 --> 00:04:37.734
Like, like, I did not --
-Did he not?

00:04:37.734 --> 00:04:39.400
Did he not? Did he not?
Did he not?

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:40.734
-Look. Look. Look.
-Did he not?

00:04:40.734 --> 00:04:44.267
-Did he not? Did he not?
Did he not? Did he not?

00:04:44.267 --> 00:04:48.400
Did he not? Did he not?
Did he not?

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:49.901
[ Laughter ]

00:04:49.901 --> 00:04:53.968
-Look, you're trying
to control it, though.

00:04:53.968 --> 00:04:55.868
-Look. I've let you speak.

00:04:55.868 --> 00:04:59.234
And I let...him speak.

00:04:59.234 --> 00:05:01.100
-I'm just saying,
the way you're saying it

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:04.033
is still rubbing us
the wrong way.

00:05:04.033 --> 00:05:05.400
[ Laughter ]

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:07.634
-It's -- It's --
It's rubbing you wrong?!

00:05:07.634 --> 00:05:10.367
Rubbing you wrong?!
-Oh, my gosh. Thank you.

00:05:10.367 --> 00:05:12.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:15.868 --> 00:05:18.434
-Questlove and Tariq, everyone.

00:05:18.434 --> 00:05:19.901
Thank you.

00:05:19.901 --> 00:05:24.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:24.100 --> 00:05:25.934
-No. No. No.

00:05:25.934 --> 00:05:27.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:27.601 --> 00:05:29.300
-Switching gears...

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:32.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:32.567 --> 00:05:35.968
Thank you. Switching gears...

00:05:35.968 --> 00:05:40.100
Switching gears...
I read that over -- Very nice.

00:05:40.100 --> 00:05:43.067
I read that over the next
few months Toys "R" Us --

00:05:43.067 --> 00:05:45.400
Toys "R" Us will open
inside every Macy's store

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:47.100
across the country.

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:49.400
Yeah. Yeah.

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:53.200
They've combined a department
store with a toy store,

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:56.467
or as I like to call it,
a Target.

00:05:56.467 --> 00:05:58.400
Well, get this.
Apparently due to inflation,

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:00.501
I don't know
if you guys heard this.

00:06:00.501 --> 00:06:03.667
Consumers...
-I didn't hear. What is it?

00:06:03.667 --> 00:06:06.267
-Consumers are cutting back
on chocolate purchases.

00:06:06.267 --> 00:06:07.434
-What?!
-Yeah.

00:06:07.434 --> 00:06:08.667
Well, I guess now that explains

00:06:08.667 --> 00:06:10.434
the new Whitman's Sampler
commercial I just saw.

00:06:10.434 --> 00:06:12.567
Check this out.
-At times like these,

00:06:12.567 --> 00:06:14.267
you need chocolate
you can't resist,

00:06:14.267 --> 00:06:15.567
Which is why we're releasing

00:06:15.567 --> 00:06:18.000
our brand-new Whitman's Sampler:
No Bull [Bleep],

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:20.167
without all that unnecessary
crap everyone hates.

00:06:20.167 --> 00:06:22.601
So say goodbye to cherry
cordials that taste like

00:06:22.601 --> 00:06:24.534
fruit dipped in
your grandmother's perfume

00:06:24.534 --> 00:06:27.200
or coconut chews that leak out
a weird milky goo.

00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:30.234
And let's be straight-up --
no one likes nougat.

00:06:30.234 --> 00:06:32.200
Whitman's Sampler:
No Bull [Bleep].

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:34.234
You want bull [bleep],
call Russell Stover.

00:06:34.234 --> 00:06:38.334
-I mean, that's just --
Can you believe I saw that?

00:06:38.334 --> 00:06:41.901
-Odd. Indeed.
-Hey, guys.

00:06:41.901 --> 00:06:43.901
I saw that today
former New York City mayor

00:06:43.901 --> 00:06:47.067
Bill de Blasio dropped
out of the race for Congress.

00:06:47.067 --> 00:06:48.734
Yeah. He --

00:06:48.734 --> 00:06:51.667
[ Applause ]

00:06:51.667 --> 00:06:54.200
The hardest part was breaking
the news to his supporter.

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:57.467
[ Laughter ]

00:06:57.467 --> 00:06:58.968
You guys see this?

00:06:58.968 --> 00:07:01.868
A man in Wisconsin tried to use
a brick to rob a Kay Jewelers.

00:07:01.868 --> 00:07:03.467
Did you see this?

00:07:03.467 --> 00:07:06.133
But it did not go as planned.
Take a look at this.

00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:12.534
[ Laughter ]

00:07:26.167 --> 00:07:27.934
-Yeah.

00:07:27.934 --> 00:07:30.601
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:30.601 --> 00:07:32.200
After...

00:07:32.200 --> 00:07:34.067
After a few minutes, even
the security guard was like,

00:07:34.067 --> 00:07:36.300
"Here, let me try."

